## Authentication Flow

1. User visits frontend and is redirected to GitHub OAuth
2. After successful authentication, user session is created
3. VS Code extension exchanges GitHub token for service JWT
4. Service JWT is used for all API requests from extension
5. Web interface uses session cookies for authentication

## Real-time Updates

### Polling Strategy
- Chat list polls every 5 seconds for new sessions
- Chat content polls every 3 seconds for updates
- Command polling from extension every few seconds

### Data Flow
1. Extension sends chat data to `/api/chat/update`
2. Data stored in Redis with user-scoped keys
3. Web interface polls endpoints for updates
4. UI automatically refreshes with new content

## Security Features

- **User Isolation**: Redis keys scoped by user ID
- **JWT Authentication**: Service tokens for extension API access
- **Session Management**: Secure cookie-based sessions for web interface
- **CORS Configuration**: Proper cross-origin request handling
- **HTML Sanitization**: Safe rendering of chat content

## Styling & UI

- **Tailwind CSS**: Utility-first CSS framework
- **Shadcn/UI**: High-quality component library
- **Dark Mode**: Automatic theme switching support
- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-first approach with proper breakpoints
- **Typography**: Prose styling for chat content display

## Dependencies

### Core Framework
- Next.js 14 with App Router
- React 19 with TypeScript
- Auth.js for authentication

### Styling & UI
- Tailwind CSS + Shadcn/UI components
- Lucide React icons
- Framer Motion for animations

### Data & Storage
- Redis/Vercel KV for real-time data
- Drizzle ORM + PostgreSQL (optional)
- Zod for runtime validation




